<title>USA: US West unit debt offer grows to $3.5 bln.</title>
<headline>US West unit debt offer grows to $3.5 bln.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>US West Inc's US West Capital Funding has increased its debt offering to $3.5 billion from a planned $2.0 billion in response to strong investor demand, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The US West Capital deal has been launched at a size of $3.5 billion and is expected to price tomorrow,&quot; said one high-grade syndicate source.</p>
<p>On Tuesday the deal was rumored to have gone to $2.25 billion with the addition of a fifth tranche, consisting of a century bond, dealers said.</p>
</text>
